<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Wolaita</h1><p class="st-meta">1250 CE – 1894 CE (approx.) · capital Dalbo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A long-lived kingdom of southern Ethiopia whose last king, Kawo Tona, fought a costly war against Menelik II's expanding empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Wolaita traditions describe a first royal dynasty, the Wolaita Malla, which ruled from about the 13th century, followed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tigray">Tigre</a> dynasty, founded according to tradition by a northerner who settled in the region and seized power in the 17th century. The kingdom lay between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omo-river">Omo</a> river and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-african-rift">Rift Valley</a> lakes, south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurage-people">Gurage</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hadiya-sultanate">Hadiya</a> lands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The king, or kawo, ruled from fortified residences such as Dalbo with a court of officials and a council of clan leaders, and the kingdom was defended by ditches and walls. Farming of ensete (false banana), cereals and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> supported a dense population. Wolaita traded cloth, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and slaves and absorbed neighbouring peoples. Traditional religion coexisted with older Christian traces.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1894 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> invaded with a large army, and after fierce resistance <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kawo-tona-gaga">Kawo Tona Gaga</a> was wounded and captured. Tens of thousands died or were enslaved, and Wolaita was annexed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>. Its memory remains strong in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolaita-zone">Wolaita Zone</a> today.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-wolaita.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Wolaita" width="320" height="221"><figcaption>Image: El Bux · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wolayta_traditional_pattern.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1250 CE – 1894 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dalbo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kawo Tona Gaga</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Wolaytta</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Wolaita, Wolayta, Welayta</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1572&amp;focus=kingdom-of-wolaita" aria-label="Kingdom of Wolaita on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5727 1920 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Wolaita lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6047 2176L6029 1964"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6029 1964h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6047 2176h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6047 2176h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dalbo. <a href="/atlas?year=1572&amp;focus=kingdom-of-wolaita">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

